  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Solve the quadratic equations.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x}{3}+\\dfrac{x-1}{15}=\\dfrac{2}{3}+\\dfrac{22}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-5$ or $x=6$.",
          "worked": "The restriction is $x\\ne0$. Multiply both sides by $15x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}10x^2+x(x-1)&=10x+330\\\\11x^2-11x-330&=0\\\\x^2-x-30&=0\\\\(x+5)(x-6)&=0\\\\x&=-5\\text{ or }x=6\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x}{2}+\\dfrac{x-4}{x-4}=\\dfrac{x}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-6$.",
          "worked": "The restriction is $x\\ne4$, so $\\dfrac{x-4}{x-4}=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{2}+1&=\\frac{x}{3}\\\\3x+6&=2x\\\\x&=-6\\end{align*}$$\nThis value satisfies the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x+1}{7}+\\dfrac{8}{x-2}=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=6$ or $x=16$.",
          "worked": "The restriction is $x\\ne2$. Multiply both sides by $7(x-2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)(x-2)+56&=21(x-2)\\\\x^2-x+54&=21x-42\\\\x^2-22x+96&=0\\\\(x-6)(x-16)&=0\\\\x&=6\\text{ or }x=16\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x-1}{x+2}-\\dfrac{x-3}{x-4}=-\\dfrac{2}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$ or $x=7$.",
          "worked": "The restrictions are $x\\ne-2,4$. Multiply both sides by $3(x+2)(x-4)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3(x-1)(x-4)-3(x-3)(x+2)&=-2(x+2)(x-4)\\\\3(x^2-5x+4)-3(x^2-x-6)&=-2(x^2-2x-8)\\\\-12x+30&=-2x^2+4x+16\\\\2x^2-16x+14&=0\\\\x^2-8x+7&=0\\\\(x-1)(x-7)&=0\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }x=7\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 83
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x(x+9)+3=x(2-3x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$ or $x=-\\dfrac34$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+9x+3&=2x-3x^2\\\\4x^2+7x+3&=0\\\\4x^2+4x+3x+3&=0\\\\4x(x+1)+3(x+1)&=0\\\\(4x+3)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac34\\text{ or }x=-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 53
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$3x(x-2)=x(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=\\dfrac72$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x^2-6x&=x^2+x\\\\2x^2-7x&=0\\\\x(2x-7)&=0\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }x=\\frac72\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 41
      }
    ]
  },
